{title: 448 - O, When Shall I See Jesus}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #448 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Em}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 448}
{meta: category Early Advent - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Em]O when shall I see Jesus, and [D]reign with Him above,
And shall [Em]hear the trumpet [Am]sound in that [Em]morning?
[Bm7]And [Em]from that flowing fountain drink [D]everlasting love!
[F]And shall [G]hear the [Em]trumpet [A]sound in [Am]that [Em]morning?
O, shout, [D]glo[G]ry! For [D]I shall [G]mount above the [C]skies,
[Em]When I [D]hear the [Em]trumpet [Am]sound in that [Em]morning.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Em]O, shout, glory! For I [D]shall mount above the skies,
[Em]When I hear [Am]the trumpet sound [Em]in that morning.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Em]Gird on the gospel armor [D]of faith and hope and love,
[Em]And you'll hear [Am]the trumpet sound [Em]in that morning.
[Bm7]And when the [Em]combat's ended He'll [D]carry you above,
[F]And [G]you'll hear [Em]the [A]trumpet sound [Am]in [Em]that morning.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Em]Our ears shall hear with [D]transport the host of heaven sing,
[Em]And shall hear [Am]the trumpet sound [Em]in that morning.
[Bm7]Our tongues shall [Em]chant the glories [D]of our immortal King.
[F]And [G]shall hear [Em]the [A]trumpet sound [Am]in [Em]that morning,
{end_of_verse}
